    "notes": "Observed from six intake photos. Gilt 18-size movement with full-plate architecture and engraved balance cock. Case shows age-related tarnish, scratching and grime. Dial appears substantially intact in the supplied views, with scattered surface marks; inspect under magnification for hairlines/chips before final condition grading. The SAFETY PINION marking refers to Elgin's train protection arrangement and is unrelated to the reported balance-wheel wobble.",
    "history": "Grade 249 was Elgin's 18-size, 17-jewel hunting Model 4, produced 1900-1904 in about 31,000 examples. Period catalog evidence describes it as gilt, screw-set jeweled, stem wound and lever set, adjusted, with compensation balance, quick train, straight-line escapement, exposed pallets, sunk seconds dial and dust ring. A nearby documented Grade 249 serial (9729093) is dated 1903, supporting a circa-1903 date for serial 9826010.",
